{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryLogBound","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefinite"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_below_of_gt_two_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_below_of_gt_two_log","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L198-L212","doc":"**The pinned form.** With `b_pp = q²/[2]_q`, `b_nn = q⁻²/[2]_q`, the cap is\nexactly `2 ln q` (`half_splitting_pinned`), so any law whose slope exceeds\n`2 ln q` — which is what supplying the SEMF `a_A` requires, by\n`bondSum_wellMixed_symmetry` — has its interface strictly below `b_nn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_below_of_gt_convexCap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_below_of_gt_convexCap","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L179-L196","doc":"**Beating the convex cap forces the interface below *both* like-species\nbonds.** If `δ` exceeds `(ln b_pp - ln b_nn)/2` then `b_pn < b_nn`: the p–n bond\nfactor is strictly smaller than the smaller like-species factor, so it is not a\nconvex combination of them and is not derived by\n`SymmetrySignAmGm.weight_of_convention`. No sign hypothesis is used, so class B\ndoes not change this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.classB_rescaled_symmetryCoeff_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.classB_rescaled_symmetryCoeff_le","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L157-L175","doc":"**The same cap after the class-B rescaling.** Rescale all three pinned bonds\nby any `c > 0` — in particular by one large enough to make every energy negative\n(`exists_bondRescale_all_energies_neg`) — and the bound is *the same number*.\nClass B's cap equals the positive class's cap, identically, not approximately. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.classB_symmetryCoeff_le_of_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.classB_symmetryCoeff_le_of_convex","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L144-L155","doc":"**Invariant (1) holds for class B: the symmetry coefficient of any convex\ninterface is at most `(μ/4)·2 ln q`, with no sign hypothesis on any energy.**\nComposition of `energySlope_convex_le_two_log` with the generic monotonicity\n`symmetryCoeff_le_of_energySlope_le`. On a well-mixed degree-`k` graph\n(`μ = k/A`, `bondSum_wellMixed_symmetry`) this is `a_A^eff ≤ (k/2)·E₀·ln q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.interface_pos","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L138-L142","doc":"The convex interface of a positive pair of like-species bonds is positive —\nneeded to rescale it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.pinned_bnn_le_bpp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.pinned_bnn_le_bpp","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L126-L136","doc":"The pinned like-species ordering `b_nn ≤ b_pp`, extracted from\n`BondCutSymmetryLogBound.energySlope_convex_le_two_log`'s proof so the class-B\nstatements below can reuse it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.exists_bondRescale_all_energies_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.exists_bondRescale_all_energies_neg","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L98-L122","doc":"**Class B is reachable from any positive law, at zero cost in `δ`.** For any\npositive bond factors there is a common scale `c > 0` making all three energies\nstrictly negative — every bond repulsive, `bondSum_nonneg` fully escaped — while\nthe p–n slope, and hence the whole symmetry coefficient, is *identically* the\none before the rescaling.\n\nSo the cheapest and most natural way into class B changes nothing the symmetry\nterm sees. Whatever class B can do, it cannot do it uniformly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.one_lt_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.one_lt_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L86-L96","doc":"`(1/x + 1/y + 1/z)·x = 1 + x/y + x/z > 1` for positive `x, y, z`: the scale\nused below to push every bond factor above one. Stated rather than kept private\nso the axiom audit covers it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.energySlope_bondRescale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.energySlope_bondRescale","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L73-L84","doc":"**Rescaling all three bond factors by a common `c > 0` leaves `δ`\nunchanged.** `ln (c·b) = ln c + ln b`, so every energy shifts by `-ln c` and the\ngeneric `energySlope_energyShift` applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.energy_neg_iff_one_lt_bond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.energy_neg_iff_one_lt_bond","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/BondCutSymmetryNoSignDefiniteLogBound.lean#L56-L69","doc":"**Class B is `b > 1`.** A bond energy `e = -ln b` is negative — repulsive —\nexactly when its bond factor exceeds one. This is the definition the enumeration\nin bean `qou-brng` gives, made checkable against a derived number. ","signatureChunk":0}]}